---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ToConfirm from '../components/ToConfirm.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<Base title={`Privacy notice | ${site.name}`} description="How My Maths Mentor uses the personal information you share through this website.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <span class="kicker">Your information</span>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="container container--narrow prose">
    <p class="lede">
      This notice explains what personal information My Maths Mentor collects when you use this website or get in
      touch, and how it’s used.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      My Maths Mentor is a maths mentoring service run by {site.owner} in {site.locality}. {site.owner} is responsible
      for the personal information described here. You can get in touch at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <ToConfirm>
      <p>Check whether My Maths Mentor needs to pay the ICO data protection fee, and add the registration number here if so.</p>
    </ToConfirm>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>When you send an enquiry through the form, we receive:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your name and email address</li>
      <li>your child’s school year or stage</li>
      <li>your preferred days and times, if you give them</li>
      <li>anything you write in your message</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We ask you not to include your child’s full name, date of birth or medical details in the form. If you email us
      directly, we receive your email address and whatever your email contains.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      We use your information to reply to your enquiry and, if you decide to go ahead, to arrange sessions. We don’t
      sell it or share it for marketing.
    </p>
    <p>
      Under UK data protection law, we rely on our legitimate interest in responding to enquiries, and on taking steps
      you’ve asked for before arranging sessions.
    </p>

    <h2>Who else handles it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Formspree</strong> receives enquiry form submissions and passes them to us by email. Formspree is based
        in the United States. See <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/">Formspree’s privacy policy</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> hosts this website. GitHub records visitors’ IP addresses for security purposes.
        See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <ToConfirm>
      <p>Name the email provider used for {site.email} once it’s set up.</p>
    </ToConfirm>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Enquiries that don’t lead to sessions are deleted after 6 months.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
    <p>
      This website doesn’t use cookies, analytics or advertising trackers. The fonts are served from this website
      itself, so viewing a page doesn’t share your details with a font provider.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask to see the information we hold about you, ask us to correct or delete it, or object to how we use it.
      Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we’ll respond within one month.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you’re unhappy with how we’ve handled your information, you can complain to the Information Commissioner’s
      Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/">ico.org.uk</a>.
    </p>

    <ToConfirm>
      <p>Add the date this notice takes effect (the launch date), for example “This notice was last updated on …”.</p>
    </ToConfirm>

    <p><a href={url('/')}>Back to the home page</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
